# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

## Summary
Successfully implemented Vercel Web Analytics for the React/Vite application following the official Vercel documentation guidelines for React applications.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 1.6.1
- Updated package.json to include the new dependency
- Updated package-lock.json with the new package and its dependencies

### 2. Analytics Integration (src/App.jsx)
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/react";`
- Integrated the `<Analytics />` component at the root level of the App component
- Placed the component inside the fragment before the Routes component to ensure it tracks all pages

### 3. Verification
- Build completed successfully without errors
- No new linting errors introduced in App.jsx
- All changes follow React best practices and existing code structure

## Implementation Details

The Analytics component was added to `src/App.jsx` following the pattern for React applications:
- Imported from `@vercel/analytics/react` package
- Positioned at the top level to ensure it loads on all routes
- Works seamlessly with the existing React Router setup (student, faculty, and admin routes)

## Technical Notes

1. **Framework**: React with Vite build system
2. **Integration Type**: React component wrapper (provides route support)
3. **Placement**: Root App component ensures tracking across all user roles (student, faculty, admin)
4. **Build**: Verified successful build with no breaking changes
5. **Linting**: No new linting errors introduced

## Next Steps for Deployment

To complete the Vercel Web Analytics setup:

1. **Enable Web Analytics on Vercel Dashboard**:
   - Go to the project on Vercel dashboard
   - Click the "Analytics" tab
   - Click "Enable" in the dialog
   - This will add new routes scoped at `/_vercel/insights/*`

2. **Deploy to Vercel**:
   - Deploy using `vercel deploy` or through Git integration
   - Once deployed, analytics will automatically start tracking visitors

3. **Verify Installation**:
   - After deployment, visit any page of the app
   - Open browser DevTools → Network tab
   - Look for a Fetch/XHR request to `/_vercel/insights/view`
   - If present, analytics is working correctly

4. **View Analytics Data**:
   - Go to Vercel dashboard → Project → Analytics tab
   - Data will appear after users visit the site

## Files Modified
- `Frontend/src/App.jsx` - Added Analytics component and import
- `Frontend/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `Frontend/package-lock.json` - Updated with new package dependencies
